.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines matching a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function searches each line of the file pointed to by
.I fp
for the substring
.I search_str,
and stores pointers to the matching lines in the array pointed to by
.I matches.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
